AI Study Hub database migrations
================================

Run from the repository root with the project virtual environment active:

    python -m flask --app run.py db upgrade
    python -m flask --app run.py db current

The configured directory is alembic/. env.py is Alembic's migration runner,
not the secret .env file. alembic.ini contains logging settings only; Flask
supplies the configured database connection.

The full upgrade chain is:

    caa005233e4d  initial users, topics, notes, conversations, messages, progress
    8e7b3d2a1c44  PDF filename and study-plan tables
    0a6f912e7b30  flashcards (required before flashcard_progress)
    1f4296c2362e  flashcard_progress
    b4e3c8f2a921  study events, quiz history, floating-point review progress
    c912d45b810e  assistant message request IDs
    d8a17c09e452  study-plan completed flag used by the existing model

The first two revisions were recovered from the old migrations/ directory.
The prerequisite of 1f4296c2362e was repaired so an empty database can be
created in foreign-key order. Existing revision IDs were retained. Databases
already at 1f4296c2362e or later do not rerun the recovered prerequisites;
those existing databases must already contain their core tables. The final
revision accepts the completed column if a model-created database has it.

Do not regenerate or stamp migration history to fix setup errors. Check
the database's current revision and schema first. Existing databases with
tables but no Alembic revision need a separate reconciliation and backup;
this clean-install repair does not automatically adopt arbitrary schemas.

SQLite upgrades are regression-tested, including row preservation during
the Integer-to-Float batch alteration. Test MySQL against a disposable
database before applying the upgrade to valuable data. Downgrades through
study-history revisions are intentionally blocked to protect saved history.

Include every setup file and revision in Git. Current repository ignore
rules hide some migration files, so explicitly include them when committing:

    git add -f -- alembic/README alembic/env.py alembic/alembic.ini alembic/script.py.mako alembic/versions/*.py

Never add the secret .env file or database files with this command.
